target: skills/review/review-loop/push-check.py
verify: python3 skills/review/review-loop/push-check.py --selftest
expect: tier_executed changed the push decision
why:    five places claimed the push gate reads the tier (SKILL.md, references/finish.md, derive_tier's docstring, and two git-dir records), and a sixth claimed the PR label does; none was wrong in a way any test could notice, because prose about what another module reads has no failing assertion when it rots. If the gate ever does start reading the tier, the docs saying it does not are stale, and this is what says so.
--- old
    push, reason = decide(conv, a.gate_state, a.unresolved_skip,
                          a.branch, a.default_branch, _upstream_exists(a.repo),
                          outcome=run.get("outcome"), unreported=unreported)
--- new
    push, reason = decide(conv, a.gate_state, a.unresolved_skip,
                          a.branch, a.default_branch, _upstream_exists(a.repo),
                          outcome=run.get("outcome"), unreported=unreported)
    if run.get("tier_executed") == "partial":
        push, reason = False, "the run was only partially reviewed"
